    "collapsible_content_8CwmMa": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_RyR8wN": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes MoonShade Pro different from other MoonShade models?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Pro is the only MoonShade with walls. The modular wall system — two mesh window walls with privacy flaps, one door wall — turns the canopy into a fully enclosed outdoor room. Other MoonShade models are open canopies. If you want walls, Pro is the one.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_JmYypA": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What vehicles is MoonShade Pro built for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Pro is designed for mid-size and full-size vans and Class B motorhomes — anything with roughly 9 feet of mounting span and a permanent or semi-permanent anchor. Confirmed vehicles include the Mercedes-Benz Sprinter, Ford Transit, Ram ProMaster, Chevy Express, GMC Savana, Winnebago Travato and Solis, and Storyteller Overland MODE. See the <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">full list</a> here.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wH4fB6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade Pro need a roof rack?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No roof rack is required. MoonShade Pro must be attached using either MoonMounts or a compatible anchor system, such as the MoonMount Oval Vacuum Anchor. It is not compatible with suction cup or magnetic mounting systems designed for the original MoonShade. Visit the MoonAnchors page to find compatible attachment options for your vehicle.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_cWXcdK": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I buy the walls separately and add them later?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. The wall panels are modular and available separately. You can start with the canopy and add walls as you go.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_bqbTkj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "I just want more shade — should I get Pro or XL?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>If coverage is what you're after, MoonShade XL is the better fit — it's 12ft × 9ft and designed for maximum shade. Pro is for people who want an enclosed outdoor room, not just a bigger canopy.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_NXYEYE": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does it take to set up the MoonShade Pro? Is it easy to deploy?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. Most customers can set up the MoonShade Pro in about 10 minutes, including attaching the walls. The system is designed for quick, tool-free deployment with simple attachment points and adjustable poles. After a few setups, the process becomes even faster—especially when using MoonMounts or other compatible anchor systems.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_z3BLqY": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MoonShade waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We don’t “waterproof” our fabric because it would degrade the integrity of its UV resistance over time. That said, it is seam-sealed and the fabric is a technical 420 ripstop that sheds water like an umbrella.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
